#---
# purpose: "a child's reply that matches the parent's parked receive is copied by the child into a gift the parent grafts at its next dispatch, so each list cell that crosses is copied once, by its sender; the earlier unmatched 50000-element log is gifted whole and waits in the mailbox"
#---
#
# The parent parks on `{:ok, xs}` before the child runs. The child's first
# send is a 50000-element list the matcher rejects: the child copies the whole
# message into a gift and queues it on the parent without waking it. The second
# send matches: the child runs the matcher, copies the three bound cells into a
# gift, and wakes the parent once. The parent grafts both gifts when it is
# dispatched, before any of its code runs, and copies nothing: the run's
# `runtime::copy_list_cell` site counts 50003 cells, the 50000 and the 3 the
# child's two gifts carry. The log is already in the mailbox when the second
# receive asks for it.
def main() do
  parent = self()
  spawn(fn () ->
    send(parent, {:log, Enum.to_list(1..50000)})
    send(parent, {:ok, [1, 2, 3]})
  end)
  receive do
    {:ok, xs} -> dbg(xs)
  end
  receive do
    {:log, log} -> dbg(Enum.count(log))
  end
end
